WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
(bright music)

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:04.260
- [Zoe] In Southern Texas,

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.300
just a few miles from the Mexico border,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.660
and almost three hours from San Antonio,

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.873
sits the quiet town of Del Rio.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.570
Texas is a place where local politics

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.493
are often steeped in anti-LGBT rhetoric.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.750
But in a wave of change,

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.003
Del Rio elected its first
openly gay mayor in 2018.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.280
I'm Zoe Saldana from BESE,

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.170
and I'm teaming up with Great Big Story

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.070
to shine a light on
American Latinx excellence

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.300
around the country.

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:42.230
(lighthearted music)

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.563
- I'm Bruno Lozano, and I'm
the mayor of Del Rio, Texas.

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:49.200
I was born and raised
here in Del Rio, Texas.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.780
I joined the military when I was 21.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.510
I served in the Air Force
under Don't Ask, Don't Tell.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.690
I left and lived in big cities,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.253
and I came back to Del Rio, Texas in 2016.

00:01:02.765 --> 00:01:04.350
(poignant music)

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:08.250
I was not openly gay until
maybe I was 15 years old.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.890
Growing up, I was bullied,
because I was flamboyant.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.690
I was feminine; I was more effeminate.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:16.110
And being feminine is
considered a weakness

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:19.733
in the machismo culture that
permeates this entire area.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.813
But the same people who bullied
me voted me into office.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:29.380
- [Zoe] Bruno ran on a platform
built on infrastructure,

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.290
employment and tourism.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.290
Despite running against an incumbent,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:37.430
Bruno won his election
with 62% of the vote.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.790
- I decided to run for office

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.620
because I've always believed in Del Rio

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.240
and its full potential.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.330
On my campaign trail, I did
not run as a gay politician

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.163
or as a gay mayor.

00:01:46.163 --> 00:01:49.810
I ran as Bruno, who happens to
be all of these other things.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.460
Miss Carpenter, you may now have the floor

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.160
to speak for three minutes.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.090
You can win people's hearts over

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.750
as long as you are true to yourself

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.863
and true to your mind and goal.

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:02.423
(gavel bangs)

00:02:02.423 --> 00:02:05.770
(poignant music)

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.180
- [Zoe] Since becoming mayor,

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.290
Bruno has written support
resolutions for local initiatives,

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.080
appointed members to the Parks Committee

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.960
and Housing Authority,
but most importantly,

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.283
he has created a space
for people like him.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.990
- [Bruno] For me, the future
of Del Rio is being a place

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.963
where people are welcome, are
inviting, and are different.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.440
I left looking for acceptance

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.810
and looking for people like me,

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.410
but I chose to come back to Del Rio

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.670
because my community is here,

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.610
and it's important for
people who are different,

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.543
like myself, to be visible.

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:42.700
You can be gay, you can be different,

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.430
and you can still run for
office here in Del Rio, Texas,

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.203
and win an election.

00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:55.721
(bright tones)

